          "text": "The issue is the method\u2019s `private` visibility. Although it works for `MultiKey` itself, a private `readResolve()` is not inherited by subclasses. Deserializing a subclass may therefore leave the transient cached hash code at its default value of `0`.\n\nMake the method `protected` so Java serialization can use it for subclasses as well:\n\n```java\n/**\n * Recalculates the hash code after deserialization. The hash codes of some\n * keys might have changed (identity-based hash codes are only stable\n * within the same process).\n *\n * @return this instance with its hash code recalculated\n */\nprotected Object readResolve() {\n    calculateHashCode(keys);\n    return this;\n}\n```\n\nThe recalculation and return value are already correct; the visibility is what needs fixing."
        }
      ],
